 "mundo": "campo",
 "autor": "claude",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your four cows make fifty kilos of manure a day, and the farm stinks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Flies everywhere. And you're still buying gas to cook.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you dump the manure into a pit and mix it with water.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Problem solved? Not really. The open pit stinks even worse.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But look closely: the mud is bubbling.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Bacteria that live without air are eating the manure, and burping gas.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "About sixty percent of that gas is methane, the same fuel as in your stove.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you seal the pit under a brick dome.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now the gas collects at the top, and the smell stays inside.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add a steel drum on top that rises as gas fills it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Its weight pushes the gas down a pipe to your kitchen.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "You open the valve, and a clean blue flame lights up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the tank fills up with old, used-up slurry.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add an outlet, and every new bucket pushes old slurry out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "That slurry is one of the best fertilizers your fields will ever get.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "India has around five million of these on family farms.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a biogas digester. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
